---
description: Stop CursorUsage.exe before every local publish or release
alwaysApply: true
---

# Stop the running EXE before publish

`CursorUsage.exe` locks `dist/CursorUsage.exe` while it is running. `dotnet publish` then fails.

Before **every** local publish, rebuild, or release prep:

1. Stop the running process (`Stop-Process -Name CursorUsage -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`).
2. Then `dotnet publish` / tag / push.
3. After a local try, start `dist\CursorUsage.exe` again.

GitHub Actions builds on a runner and does not need the local EXE stopped. Stop it anyway when this machine will also publish to `dist/`.

Do not attach a locally built EXE to a GitHub Release. CI on a `v*` tag is the only ship path.
